  {"comment": "Patterns of a rib and a web re-solved at each copy (mitcad#1968): a room that narrows and deepens along X. Its floor (Sketch1 F1 on XZ, whose sketch y is -Z; Extrude1 F2, y 0 to 60, Body1 F2.b0) rises from z = 2 at x = 100 to z = 10 at x = 0: its top is z = 10 - 0.08 x, 600 x 60 = 36000 mm3. Two walls 2 thick and 30 high, slanted in plan (Sketch2 F3, Extrude2 F4 and Sketch3 F5, Extrude3 F6, joined): the inner faces y = 8.75 + 0.125 x and y = 51.25 - 0.125 x, so the room is 42.5 - 0.25 x wide; each wall adds 6000 less the 1200 inside the floor. 45600 mm3."},
  {"cmd": "sketch.create", "plane": "xz"},
  {"cmd": "sketch.add_line", "sketch": "F1", "start": [0, 0], "end": [0, -10]},
